WEBVTT

1
00:51:01.762 --> 00:51:08.762
Good morning. How good it is to be in the house of the Lord.

2
00:51:08.762 --> 00:51:12.762
When I'm not here, I really miss it.

3
00:51:12.762 --> 00:51:18.762
Today I get to talk about giving. And we do that quite often.

4
00:51:18.762 --> 00:51:22.762
But today I want to highlight two aspects of giving.

5
00:51:22.762 --> 00:51:28.762
The first aspect is that a reason to give is to go for it together.

6
00:51:28.762 --> 00:51:30.762
To share the costs together.

7
00:51:30.762 --> 00:51:36.762
Together we are a church family, a family of God.

8
00:51:36.762 --> 00:51:38.762
And together we bear the costs.

9
00:51:38.762 --> 00:51:43.762
And those who know me a little know that I love lists.

10
00:51:43.762 --> 00:51:45.762
Who here also loves lists?

11
00:51:45.762 --> 00:51:49.762
Ah look, indeed, I see a few of you.

12
00:51:49.762 --> 00:51:52.762
I love keeping lists.

13
00:51:53.762 --> 00:51:58.762
Lists. Excel sheets. I love it.

14
00:51:58.762 --> 00:52:00.762
I love keeping lists.

15
00:52:00.762 --> 00:52:03.762
And do you know what is so fun? The Bible does that too.

16
00:52:03.762 --> 00:52:07.762
There are many places in the Bible with whole lists.

17
00:52:07.762 --> 00:52:12.762
Genealogies, but also lists for the worship service of the temple.

18
00:52:12.762 --> 00:52:14.762
What was needed for it all.

19
00:52:14.762 --> 00:52:19.762
And today I have a small list from our church of what is needed.

20
00:52:19.762 --> 00:52:23.762
Per year we use 7000 liters of mazout.

21
00:52:23.762 --> 00:52:25.762
To keep it warm here.

22
00:52:25.762 --> 00:52:30.762
But we also use 15,000 kWh of electricity.

23
00:52:30.762 --> 00:52:38.762
Yes, there are no wheels behind here that you can ride on or anything to generate the electricity.

24
00:52:38.762 --> 00:52:41.762
No, we really have to pay for that, right?

25
00:52:41.762 --> 00:52:50.762
Did you know that we need a total of 3,600 cups for communion each year?

26
00:52:50.762 --> 00:52:58.762
Did you know that we brew 15,500 cups of coffee per year?

27
00:52:58.762 --> 00:53:01.762
That's a lot of liters of coffee.

28
00:53:01.762 --> 00:53:05.762
Well, I find the last two so fun.

29
00:53:05.762 --> 00:53:10.762
Did you know that the children's church hands out fresh fruit every week?

30
00:53:10.762 --> 00:53:16.762
And that we use 520 kilos of fruit per year?

31
00:53:17.762 --> 00:53:20.762
And I personally find the very best one.

32
00:53:20.762 --> 00:53:28.762
We have given away 18,360 eggs per year.

33
00:53:32.762 --> 00:53:36.762
Those are things you don't think about.

34
00:53:36.762 --> 00:53:42.762
But how cool is it to be able to give away more than 18,000 eggs to the food bank of Lommel?

35
00:53:42.762 --> 00:53:44.762
And we all carry that together.

36
00:53:44.762 --> 00:53:47.762
That all comes from one and the same pot of finances.

37
00:53:47.762 --> 00:53:49.762
That's one reason.

38
00:53:49.762 --> 00:53:54.762
The second reason is even more important, because it concerns you personally.

39
00:53:54.762 --> 00:53:59.762
The second reason is that God wants to teach us to be generous.

40
00:53:59.762 --> 00:54:01.762
Not to be tied down to something.

41
00:54:01.762 --> 00:54:05.762
Not to be greedy and to gather and hold on to things for oneself.

42
00:54:05.762 --> 00:54:08.762
In 2 Corinthians 9 it also says.

43
00:54:08.762 --> 00:54:10.762
Let's read it for a moment.

44
00:54:12.762 --> 00:54:14.762
Shall we read? Yes.

45
00:54:14.762 --> 00:54:18.762
Everyone must decide for themselves how much they want to give.

46
00:54:18.762 --> 00:54:20.762
You should know for yourself.

47
00:54:20.762 --> 00:54:22.762
And if you don't want to give, that's fine too.

48
00:54:22.762 --> 00:54:25.762
You especially shouldn't do it if you don't want to.

49
00:54:25.762 --> 00:54:28.762
And let him give cheerfully.

50
00:54:28.762 --> 00:54:31.762
For without reluctance or compulsion.

51
00:54:31.762 --> 00:54:34.762
God loves people who give with a joyful heart.

52
00:54:34.762 --> 00:54:37.762
God wants to teach us that we are not bound to that.

53
00:54:37.762 --> 00:54:42.762
Not to our belongings, not to our house, not to our car, not to our finances.

54
00:54:42.762 --> 00:54:44.762
Be free.

55
00:54:44.762 --> 00:54:46.762
For God takes care of us.

56
00:54:46.762 --> 00:54:49.762
And that is the best reason to give.

57
00:54:49.762 --> 00:54:52.762
Because He wants to change you.

58
00:54:52.762 --> 00:54:54.762
Because He cares for you.

59
00:54:54.762 --> 00:54:57.762
And we don't have to worry.

60
00:54:57.762 --> 00:55:00.762
You can give with the app, with the church app.

61
00:55:00.762 --> 00:55:03.762
You can also give via QR codes.

62
00:55:03.762 --> 00:55:06.762
They are here, but there are also cards on the chairs.

63
00:55:06.762 --> 00:55:07.762
Take a look around.

64
00:55:07.762 --> 00:55:11.762
And even if you have never given before, I would like to challenge you.

65
00:55:11.762 --> 00:55:13.762
For those two reasons.

66
00:55:13.762 --> 00:55:15.762
Yes, we are going for it together.

67
00:55:15.762 --> 00:55:17.762
We share those costs together.

68
00:55:17.762 --> 00:55:20.762
But God also wants to take care of you.

69
00:55:20.762 --> 00:55:23.762
Show that you trust Him in that.

70
00:55:23.762 --> 00:55:24.762
Amen.

71
00:55:34.762 --> 00:55:35.762
Hello.

72
00:55:35.762 --> 00:55:37.762
Am I on?

73
00:55:39.762 --> 00:55:41.762
I needed a little push to get started.

74
00:55:42.762 --> 00:55:43.762
Praise God.

75
00:55:43.762 --> 00:55:45.762
Are you ready for the Word of God?

76
00:55:47.762 --> 00:55:48.762
Are you all comfortable?

77
00:55:48.762 --> 00:55:52.762
Or do we enjoy standing in honor of the Lord and for the Word of God.

78
00:55:52.762 --> 00:55:54.762
And to receive it.

79
00:55:54.762 --> 00:55:55.762
In prayer.

80
00:55:57.762 --> 00:55:58.762
All grumbling.

81
00:55:58.762 --> 00:55:59.762
Yes, yes, yes.

82
00:55:59.762 --> 00:56:00.762
This is how it should be.

83
00:56:01.762 --> 00:56:02.762
Shall we close our eyes?

84
00:56:02.762 --> 00:56:04.762
Shall we receive the Word in faith?

85
00:56:04.762 --> 00:56:06.762
Lord, I thank you for your Word.

86
00:56:06.762 --> 00:56:08.762
Lord, I thank you that we have the Bible.

87
00:56:08.762 --> 00:56:10.762
It is an absolute miracle.

88
00:56:10.762 --> 00:56:13.762
It is a miracle that we have the written Word of God.

89
00:56:13.762 --> 00:56:17.762
It is a miracle that people took the time.

90
00:56:17.762 --> 00:56:22.762
To be led by the Holy Spirit to write down the revelations of God.

91
00:56:22.762 --> 00:56:23.762
It is a miracle.

92
00:56:23.762 --> 00:56:25.762
It is a miracle, it is a miracle.

93
00:56:25.762 --> 00:56:28.762
That we have received the written Word of God.

94
00:56:28.762 --> 00:56:31.762
It is a miracle that we have the written Word of God.

95
00:56:31.762 --> 00:56:36.762
There were people in the Old Testament in the Bible who did not have the Word of God.

96
00:56:36.762 --> 00:56:39.762
And they had to rely on pure revelation and guidance.

97
00:56:39.762 --> 00:56:42.762
We have received the written Word from God.

98
00:56:42.762 --> 00:56:44.762
That is a miracle.

99
00:56:44.762 --> 00:56:47.762
And I want us to treat that miracle with reverence.

100
00:56:47.762 --> 00:56:50.762
And that we will eat the Word of God.

101
00:56:50.762 --> 00:56:51.762
In the name of Jesus.

102
00:56:51.762 --> 00:56:52.762
Amen.

103
00:56:52.762 --> 00:56:53.762
Amen.

104
00:56:53.762 --> 00:56:54.762
Not so good?

105
00:56:59.762 --> 00:57:00.762
Go ahead and sit down.

106
00:57:10.762 --> 00:57:16.762
I had to laugh yesterday about the concept of eating God's Word.

107
00:57:16.762 --> 00:57:18.762
That's a biblical concept, right?

108
00:57:18.762 --> 00:57:19.762
Eating the scroll, right?

109
00:57:19.762 --> 00:57:20.762
Eating God's Word.

110
00:57:20.762 --> 00:57:21.762
That's biblical, right?

111
00:57:21.762 --> 00:57:23.762
We recently got a dog.

112
00:57:23.762 --> 00:57:28.762
And yesterday he was eating the Bible.

113
00:57:28.762 --> 00:57:33.762
So I came home and Rocky was eating a page.

114
00:57:33.762 --> 00:57:34.762
Yeah!

115
00:57:34.762 --> 00:57:35.762
Good boy.

116
00:57:35.762 --> 00:57:38.762
I found it quite funny.

117
00:57:38.762 --> 00:57:39.762
Hallelujah.

118
00:57:39.762 --> 00:57:41.762
Let's start with something funny.

119
00:57:41.762 --> 00:57:43.762
Let's start with something nice.

120
00:57:43.762 --> 00:57:45.762
I always enjoy being in church.

121
00:57:45.762 --> 00:57:47.762
But let's start with something light-hearted.

122
00:57:47.762 --> 00:57:49.762
Just a trivia.

123
00:57:50.762 --> 00:57:52.762
Everyone except Agnes may respond.

124
00:57:58.762 --> 00:58:04.762
The Bible in the Old Testament is...

125
00:58:04.762 --> 00:58:06.762
You can give it different words.

126
00:58:06.762 --> 00:58:08.762
I will show a few words.

127
00:58:08.762 --> 00:58:13.762
The Bible in the Old Testament is a foreshadow...

128
00:58:13.762 --> 00:58:14.762
I will show a few words.

129
00:58:14.762 --> 00:58:22.762
The Bible in the Old Testament is a foreshadow of Jesus and the Kingdom of God.

130
00:58:22.762 --> 00:58:30.762
The Bible in the Old Testament is a type of Jesus and the Kingdom of God.

131
00:58:30.762 --> 00:58:32.762
That is why we sometimes talk about the study.

132
00:58:32.762 --> 00:58:33.762
That is typology.

133
00:58:33.762 --> 00:58:34.762
Then you talk.

134
00:58:34.762 --> 00:58:35.762
Oh yes, this is a type.

135
00:58:35.762 --> 00:58:36.762
A foreshadow.

136
00:58:36.762 --> 00:58:42.762
A foreshadow is like when there is a lamp, when the sun is behind you and you walk.

137
00:58:42.762 --> 00:58:45.762
You can't see it, because something is in the way.

138
00:58:45.762 --> 00:58:46.762
But then you have a foreshadow.

139
00:58:46.762 --> 00:58:48.762
You see that something is coming.

140
00:58:48.762 --> 00:58:49.762
You see that on the ground.

141
00:58:49.762 --> 00:58:54.762
And that silhouette is literally the same as what is to come.

142
00:58:54.762 --> 00:58:56.762
So it is literally the same, but it is not yet.

143
00:58:56.762 --> 00:58:58.762
Do you understand what I mean?

144
00:58:58.762 --> 00:59:03.762
I personally find the word foreshadow from the Old Testament the most beautiful word.

145
00:59:05.762 --> 00:59:07.762
I also love the word symbol.

146
00:59:08.762 --> 00:59:14.762
Only for the western mind, you have to be careful how you interpret symbol.

147
00:59:14.762 --> 00:59:18.762
Because I find symbol immensely powerful.

148
00:59:18.762 --> 00:59:26.762
For me, I even find the word symbol sometimes more powerful than the symbol itself.

149
00:59:26.762 --> 00:59:29.762
A wedding ring is a symbol of marriage.

150
00:59:29.762 --> 00:59:33.762
The ring itself, well, a few hundred euros or a thousand euros, whatever.

151
00:59:33.762 --> 00:59:36.762
But the symbol is more powerful than the ring itself.

152
00:59:36.762 --> 00:59:44.762
The symbol is the agreement you made after coming to Jesus to remain faithful, never to leave,

153
00:59:44.762 --> 00:59:47.762
through happiness and through difficult times.

154
00:59:47.762 --> 00:59:51.762
So I think symbol is wonderful, but be careful when you use the word symbol.

155
00:59:51.762 --> 00:59:55.762
Because then some people might say, oh yes, it's all symbolic, it's all not true.

156
00:59:55.762 --> 00:59:57.762
No, the Old Testament is super true.

157
00:59:57.762 --> 01:00:00.762
Do you understand what I mean? It all really happened there in the Old Testament.

158
01:00:00.762 --> 01:00:03.762
So be careful when you say symbol.

159
01:00:03.762 --> 01:00:07.762
You can also say image of, it is an image of, that works too.

160
01:00:07.762 --> 01:00:10.762
I'll stick with that foreshadow, I find it the most beautiful.

161
01:00:10.762 --> 01:00:17.762
A foreshadow is something that actually is the silhouette, I see it here like this,

162
01:00:17.762 --> 01:00:22.762
is a silhouette of that big man Tim, quite a few kilos.

163
01:00:22.762 --> 01:00:25.762
And you see it there, yes, that is not a small boy.

164
01:00:25.762 --> 01:00:32.762
And that foreshadow is the same as what is here, but it is not.

165
01:00:32.762 --> 01:00:34.762
And that is the Old Testament.

166
01:00:34.762 --> 01:00:40.762
The Old Testament is a foreshadow of Jesus Christ and his kingdom.

167
01:00:41.762 --> 01:00:46.762
But it is very real and it is all what has seriously happened.

168
01:00:46.762 --> 01:00:55.762
And very often in the Old Testament you see natural things playing out that are super intense.

169
01:00:55.762 --> 01:01:00.762
And then you read that and think, could that be a foreshadow of the heavenly kingdom?

170
01:01:00.762 --> 01:01:01.762
Yes!

171
01:01:01.762 --> 01:01:11.762
Because by taking the Old Testament seriously, we learn how serious the kingdom of God is.

172
01:01:11.762 --> 01:01:21.762
The kingdom of God is not wishy-washy, nice and happy and let's get along and it's all good, Jesus loves you.

173
01:01:21.762 --> 01:01:25.762
The kingdom of God is the Old Testament fulfilled.

174
01:01:26.762 --> 01:01:36.762
So all the intense things you find in the Old Testament are processed in the kingdom of God and borne on the cross by King Jesus.

175
01:01:36.762 --> 01:01:38.762
To him be the glory, amen?

176
01:01:39.762 --> 01:01:44.762
Here come a few fun jokes and a few fun questions, trivia, you may shout it out loud.

177
01:01:44.762 --> 01:01:51.762
What is the foreshadow, what does it symbolize, what is the type, what is the foreshadow of Eden?

178
01:01:51.762 --> 01:01:54.762
What does Eden represent in the Bible?

179
01:01:54.762 --> 01:01:55.762
Shout it out.

180
01:01:58.762 --> 01:01:59.762
Yes?

181
01:01:59.762 --> 01:02:00.762
Yes?

182
01:02:00.762 --> 01:02:02.762
Ede, come on.

183
01:02:02.762 --> 01:02:04.762
Heaven, who said heaven?

184
01:02:04.762 --> 01:02:06.762
You will get a snicker in a moment.

185
01:02:08.762 --> 01:02:11.762
I would say a Toblerone, but I want that for myself.

186
01:02:11.762 --> 01:02:14.762
Ede represents heaven.

187
01:02:14.762 --> 01:02:16.762
What does Abraham stand for?

188
01:02:20.762 --> 01:02:21.762
Sorry?

189
01:02:21.762 --> 01:02:23.762
Patriarch, yes.

190
01:02:23.762 --> 01:02:24.762
But what does he do?

191
01:02:24.762 --> 01:02:30.762
When I say a word, a story comes to mind.

192
01:02:30.762 --> 01:02:32.762
That story is what the shadow is.

193
01:02:32.762 --> 01:02:42.762
That is why you need to learn the Bible, that when you see a name, when you see a word, when I say Ark of Noah.

194
01:02:42.762 --> 01:02:44.762
What does Noah represent then?

195
01:02:44.762 --> 01:02:46.762
What is the Ark?

196
01:02:46.762 --> 01:02:51.762
You need to think about that, because those are the shadows from which we can learn who God is.

197
01:02:52.762 --> 01:02:55.762
We can learn who God is from all those stories.

198
01:02:55.762 --> 01:03:01.762
Those stories shape our understanding of how the kingdom of God is structured.

199
01:03:01.762 --> 01:03:04.762
So to wake you up a bit and take you along.

200
01:03:04.762 --> 01:03:06.762
Abraham stands for faith.

201
01:03:06.762 --> 01:03:11.762
The Bible says Abraham believed and it was credited to him as righteousness.

202
01:03:11.762 --> 01:03:13.762
So Abraham stands for faith.

203
01:03:13.762 --> 01:03:15.762
He had no Bible.

204
01:03:15.762 --> 01:03:18.762
He did not have the letters, the letters of Paul.

205
01:03:18.762 --> 01:03:20.762
He did not have the gospel.

206
01:03:20.762 --> 01:03:23.762
The only thing he had was the call of the Holy Spirit.

207
01:03:23.762 --> 01:03:25.762
That said Abraham, Abraham come.

208
01:03:25.762 --> 01:03:31.762
And Abraham believed and he left everything he had, multimillionaire, everything he had.

209
01:03:31.762 --> 01:03:35.762
In the trade area, where commerce and art were, where it was good.

210
01:03:35.762 --> 01:03:37.762
He had everything, but there were many gods.

211
01:03:37.762 --> 01:03:43.762
And Abraham was called by God to say, hey listen, this is not where I want you to settle for.

212
01:03:43.762 --> 01:03:47.762
You may think you have everything, but if you do not have God, you have nothing.

213
01:03:47.762 --> 01:03:52.762
And so God calls Abraham and Abraham follows the call of God.

214
01:03:52.762 --> 01:03:56.762
So Abraham in the Old Testament symbolizes faith.

215
01:03:56.762 --> 01:04:00.762
So here we have Eden representing heaven, Abraham representing faith.

216
01:04:00.762 --> 01:04:04.762
Then we also have, I will go back a bit, the tree of knowledge of good and evil.

217
01:04:04.762 --> 01:04:07.762
What does that represent? It represents the law.

218
01:04:07.762 --> 01:04:10.762
Tree of knowledge of good and evil.

219
01:04:10.762 --> 01:04:14.762
Through the tree of knowledge of good and evil you know what is good and you know what is wrong.

220
01:04:14.762 --> 01:04:17.762
God says, if you do what the law says, I will give you life.

221
01:04:17.762 --> 01:04:20.762
If you do not do what the law says, then I give you death.

222
01:04:20.762 --> 01:04:23.762
So through the tree of knowledge of good and evil, which symbolizes the law.

223
01:04:23.762 --> 01:04:26.762
And through that you learn what it is.

224
01:04:26.762 --> 01:04:31.762
What does it mean, where is Joseph, the dream king?

225
01:04:31.762 --> 01:04:34.762
What does he stand for? What does Joseph mean?

226
01:04:34.762 --> 01:04:38.762
What is his Egyptian name that he ultimately received?

227
01:04:39.762 --> 01:04:44.762
What does Zafranapanea mean? Savior of heaven and earth.

228
01:04:44.762 --> 01:04:50.762
So what does Joseph mean? When you read the story of Joseph, you read the story of Jesus.

229
01:04:50.762 --> 01:04:55.762
Joseph is the first strongest typology of Jesus Christ himself.

230
01:04:55.762 --> 01:04:58.762
He was denied by his own people.

231
01:04:58.762 --> 01:05:05.762
He was in the churches, he was at the bottom of the common prison, without having done anything.

232
01:05:05.762 --> 01:05:09.762
And instead of complaining about this, he continued in faith together with God.

233
01:05:09.762 --> 01:05:12.762
And he was exalted to king of Egypt.

234
01:05:12.762 --> 01:05:15.762
Zafranapanea they proclaimed in Egypt. Why?

235
01:05:15.762 --> 01:05:18.762
Because Joseph was the savior of heaven and earth.

236
01:05:18.762 --> 01:05:21.762
Who is the savior of heaven and earth? His name is?

237
01:05:21.762 --> 01:05:25.762
Voila! So there we have a foreshadow, which is a story from the Old Testament.

238
01:05:25.762 --> 01:05:31.762
And that is why it is so important, people, that you bring your children to the foundation, to the children's church,

239
01:05:31.762 --> 01:05:36.762
so that they receive those stories and learn and learn, discipleship.

240
01:05:36.762 --> 01:05:39.762
What does Moses stand for?

241
01:05:39.762 --> 01:05:46.762
Moses stands for the law and Elijah stands for the prophets.

242
01:05:46.762 --> 01:05:50.762
But what does the prophet stand for? He stands for the voice of the Holy Spirit.

243
01:05:50.762 --> 01:05:54.762
So you have Moses standing for the law and Elijah standing for the Holy Spirit.

244
01:05:54.762 --> 01:06:00.762
That is why you had Moses and Elijah, who came to talk to Jesus about his death and resurrection.

245
01:06:00.762 --> 01:06:06.762
How beautiful is that? Jesus goes up the mountain and there are Moses and Elijah talking with Jesus.

246
01:06:06.762 --> 01:06:10.762
And Peter comes along, we are going to set up a tent here.

247
01:06:10.762 --> 01:06:15.762
